# agents.slice — user-scope memory ceiling for interactive agent CLI processes
# (claude/codex/cursor/gemini/etc) and their MCP descendants. Orchestration
# daemons use the separate automation.slice. Part of bead ez-gh-actions-0725.
#
# HOW A PROCESS JOINS THIS SLICE:
#   install.sh replaces installed agent CLI entry points with reversible
#   wrappers. Each future CLI launch delegates to agent-scoped-launch.sh,
#   which creates a named transient scope under agents.slice. Existing live
#   sessions are not killed or relaunched during installation. The explicit
#   escape hatch is AGENT_SLICE_OPT_OUT=1 for a single launch.
#
# WHY FINITE HIGH/MAX: MemoryHigh begins reclaim and throttling at the
# measured margin; MemoryMax is a final finite containment boundary. Together
# they bound both gradual pressure and runaway descendants without relying on
# an unbounded user-scope cgroup. The launcher keeps MCP descendants in this
# same scope so the aggregate budget remains enforceable.
#
# BLAST RADIUS / NORMAL PEAK / SAFE MARGIN (required by repo CLAUDE.md
# "Safety & Monitoring Principles" for any new threshold):
#   - Measured normal peak for this slice was 7.4 GiB (p95, 25-29 CLI
#     processes) in the July incident sample. MemoryHigh=10G leaves a
#     measured margin of 2.6 GiB before reclaim; MemoryMax=12G leaves 4.6 GiB
#     beyond that peak for accounting variance. Swap and task ceilings are
#     finite as well, so a runaway cannot page or fork without bound.
#   - This ceiling applies only to processes launched through the installed
#     wrappers into this slice; it has zero effect on the
#     ezgha daemon, the Colima VM, or any process not opted in.
#
# Static syntax validation only (no live start/enable performed by this
# commit): `systemd-analyze verify systemd/agents.slice`

[Unit]
Description=Interactive agent CLI processes (claude/codex/cursor/etc) — finite memory budget
Before=slices.target

[Slice]
MemoryHigh=10G
MemoryMax=12G
MemorySwapMax=2G
TasksMax=8192
MemoryAccounting=yes
